# A charge message is put on the item it is about, and only on an item Boss Pilot counts. The
# game's "Your trident only has 100 charges left!" does not say which trident, so it goes to the
# one worn, not the one in the pack; a blowpipe check with no toxic blowpipe carried (an ornament
# one, say) is not counted; a trident check names its trident.
# Facts: scenes/zulrah.scene. ItemID.TOXIC_TOTS_CHARGED (12899) is "Trident of the swamp" and
# ItemID.TOTS_CHARGED (11907) "Trident of the seas" in RuneLite's gameval. The messages are the
# game's as logged in the Weapon Charges plugin (github.com/geheur/weapon-charges, ChargedWeapon.java):
# "<col=ef1020>Your trident only has 100 charges left!</col>", "Your Trident of the seas has 100 charges.".
include /replays/scenes/zulrah.scene
item TOXIC_TOTS_CHARGED "Trident of the swamp"
item TOTS_CHARGED "Trident of the seas"
items WORN clear
items WORN TOXIC_TOTS_CHARGED 1
items INV TOTS_CHARGED 1
tick 2

chat GAMEMESSAGE "<col=ef1020>Your trident only has 100 charges left!</col>"
tick
expect saved.chargesV1 ~ "swamp"
expect saved.chargesV1 !~ "seas"

chat GAMEMESSAGE "Your Trident of the seas has 2,345 charges."
tick
expect saved.chargesV1 ~ [2345]

chat GAMEMESSAGE "Darts: <col=007f00>Adamant dart x 300</col>. Scales: <col=007f00>2,000 (12.2%)</col>."
tick
expect saved.chargesV1 !~ blowpipe
